        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: redact colon and folded bearer diagnostics",
        "body": "Closes https://github.com/openclaw/crabbox/issues/936.\n\nRedacts colon-delimited and line-folded bearer credentials in both the Go CLI and Worker diagnostic redaction paths. The maintained candidate also covers combined colon folds, optional whitespace before the colon, multiple-space separators, and already-redacted placeholders while preserving existing structured credential redaction.\n\nProof requested by ClawSweeper:\n\n```text\n$ go run .\ngo_header_colon output=\"Authorization: [redacted]\\nendpoint=https://api.example.invalid\" leaked=false\ngo_bearer_fold output=\"diagnostic Bearer [redacted] from provider\" leaked=false\n\n$ node /tmp/crabbox-proof-940/worker/worker-proof.mjs\nworker_header_colon output=\"Authorization: [redacted]\\nendpoint=https://worker.example.invalid\" leaked=false\nworker_bearer_fold output=\"diagnostic Bearer [redacted] from provider\" leaked=false\n```\n\nThe Go proof is a throwaway module under `/tmp/crabbox-proof-940/go` importing the real `github.com/openclaw/crabbox/internal/cli` helper from this branch. The Worker proof bundles a throwaway script that imports the real `worker/src/http.ts` redaction helper from this branch.\n\nMaintainer verification on exact candidate `715dbf4b7158e3fa4d3ea521c2c346b94cfadc20`:\n\n```text\ngo test ./internal/cli -run 'TestRedactDiagnosticSecrets' -count=1 -v\nPASS\n\nnpm test --prefix worker -- http.test.ts\nTest Files  1 passed (1)\nTests       43 passed (43)\n\ngo vet ./...\ngo test -race ./...\ngo build -trimpath -o bin/crabbox ./cmd/crabbox\nnode scripts/build-docs-site.mjs\nPASS\n\nnpm run format:check --prefix worker\nnpm run lint --prefix worker\nnpm run check --prefix worker\nnpm test --prefix worker\nnpm run build --prefix worker\n830 passed, 2 skipped; PASS\n\nautoreview --mode branch --base origin/main\nfindings: 0\n```\n\nThe focused Go and Worker runs execute the production redaction helpers with safe dummy credentials. They assert that ordinary, colon, folded, combined colon-folded, whitespace-before-colon, and multiple-space bearer values are absent while non-secret routing context and existing `[redacted]` placeholders remain visible. This deterministic helper has no external provider or funded resource to provision.\n",
